{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have given a thousand pieces of silver to your brother.</b> As a bride-price, according to the custom of one who takes a man's daughter or sister as a wife." "<b>Behold, it is for you a covering of the eyes.</b> A garment of many colors that women would wear for honor. For indeed the bride-price that I gave indicates your honor — that I did not take you as a zonah or as a concubine, but took you as a wife, and I would not have let you go so hastily had it not been for YHWH who was with you, and I was compelled to return you." "<b>To all who are with you.</b> Before the eyes of all who are with you and the members of your household." "<b>And with all, and you are reproved.</b> And before the eyes of all who hear, and before all present — so that she may perhaps seek to reproach you, according to the custom of women who rebuke and shame one another in matters of intimacy."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:58.011904810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}